# What must NOT enter the Cloud Run build context.
#
# **This file REPLACES the default behaviour, and that is the trap.** When no
# .gcloudignore exists, gcloud falls back to .gitignore. The moment one exists, that
# fallback stops, so an incomplete .gcloudignore silently UNPROTECTS everything
# .gitignore was covering. The first version of this file listed the corpus and the
# research folder and nothing else, which meant every secret pattern in .gitignore
# had quietly stopped applying to build uploads. A review caught it before a deploy
# carried one.
#
# The include directive restores that fallback explicitly. The patterns after it are
# deliberate duplication: the ones that would put a credential inside a container
# image pushed to a registry are worth stating here even though the include already
# covers them, because this file is the one somebody reads when asking "what does a
# build upload".

#!include:.gitignore

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Credentials. Duplicated from .gitignore on purpose, see above.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
id_rsa*
service-account*.json
application_default_credentials.json
.npmrc
.pypirc

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Material that is public-facing but must not ship inside an image
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Internal strategy documents, banned from any public artifact by the build
# constitution. An image pushed to a registry is a public artifact in every sense
# that matters.
_research/
_private/
_plan/

# Government source PDFs. Gitignored, large, and not needed at runtime: the API
# serves the GENERATED fact sheet, which travels inside the package.
data/corpus/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build noise
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.git
.venv
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
node_modules/

# `#!include:.gitignore` splices in ONLY the root .gitignore and does not recurse, which
# gcloud documents. Anything ignored solely by a NESTED .gitignore therefore enters the
# Cloud Build upload. Two directories were doing exactly that: a security scan's output,
# whose candidates file listed unfixed findings with full exploitation paths, and local
# Hypothesis state that was 235 of 455 uploaded files. Named here because the include
# cannot see them.
CLAUDE-SECURITY-*/
.hypothesis/
